  "kv_note": "kv64k_gb: f16 K+V at 65536 tokens from the GGUF header of the model's GGUF tag (attention layers only; sliding layers hold the window). MLX tags use the same value. glm-4.7-flash uses MLA, so its figure overstates. qwen3-next has no full_attention_interval key; llama.cpp defaults it to 4 (src/models/qwen3next.cpp), so 12 of 48 layers hold context.",
  "params_note": "qwen3.8-flash-next: 125B MoE parameters plus a 51B n-gram embedding table (Ollama library page); total counts all 176B in the file, 6B active. flint: 39.8B total, ~2.5B active incl. output head (Hugging Face card). ornith-1.5:122b: 10B active is inferred from its config (same layout as Qwen3.5-122B-A10B: 48 layers, 256 experts, 8 routed); the card gives no active count. nemotron-3-nano:30b and nemotron3:33b: from the tag/AA names. nemotron-3.5-bolt:74b: 74B total, 9B active (NVIDIA card and Ollama page).",
  "tag_flag_note": "tag_flag overrides flag for one tag: ornith-1.5:122b-nvfp4 (MLX) uses the ornith parser (open #16992); the 122b-q4_K_M GGUF tag has no parser. flint GGUF tags (40b-a2b-q4_1, 40b-a2b-gguf-nvfp4) require Ollama 0.40.9, stable since 2026-10-22; Recursive's NVFP4 score (TB 53.7) applies to 40b-a2b-gguf-nvfp4 only. flint is not flagged: open #19191 (integer tool arguments from history re-emitted as float strings) is in the flint renderer, not the parser, so Ranking rule 3 doesn't apply; the report cautions instead. A tag with \"mac\": false is skipped on Mac tiers: flint:40b-a2b-gguf-nvfp4 is NVFP4 GGUF, which llama.cpp b11803 (Ollama 0.40.9) can't run on Metal, nor can b11845 (Ollama 0.40.11); Recursive points Apple silicon to the Q4_1 GGUF. nemotron-3.5-bolt:74b-a9b-iq2 is NVIDIA's quantization-aware IQ2_XXS release (the only local 74B build); Ollama's page says Apple Silicon/Metal isn't supported for 74B-A9B, so \"mac\": false. Its TB 51.0 is NVIDIA's score for this build (card); its GS 30.8 is AA's, whose model page links the BF16 weights."
}
